# Forms

## Framework semantics

HTML forms in CakePHP typically use FormHelper with entities, and participate in FormProtection / CSRF middleware already configured on the Application. Forms marshal into entities via `newEntity`/`patchEntity` — not Laravel FormRequest classes.

## Required behavior

- Prefer FormHelper + entity context matching project templates.
- Keep FormProtection/CSRF enabled for cookie-session HTML state changes.
- Put field shape checks in Table validators; put persistence invariants in application rules.
- Do not invent FormRequest / Livewire form objects as CakePHP defaults.

## Anti-patterns

- csrf-formprotection-required
- Inventing FormRequest
- Duplicating validation only in the template

## Review checklist

- [ ] Form posts hit protected endpoints with project CSRF/FormProtection
- [ ] Entity marshaling uses Table APIs
- [ ] Locked/unlocked fields match FormProtection expectations when used
